│ This change adds a special case to the display_for_field function, │
│ ensuring that when the field is a JSONField and is readonly, it    │
│ uses prepare_value instead of json.dumps. This avoids the          │
│ InvalidJSONInput error and ensures the value is properly formatted │
│ as JSON. The logic is preserved for all other field types,         │
│ maintaining the original behavior for non-JSONField fields.        │
